    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n1000" root="اكل" body-key="A">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَكِلٌ</span></b>  [part. n. of <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَكِلَ</span>]. ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">نَاقَةٌ أَكِلَةٌ</span> (assumed tropical:)  <i>A she-camel experiencing an itching and annoyance in
her belly,</i> (S, K,) <i>from the growth of the hair,</i>
(S,) or <i>from the growth of the fur,</i> (K,) <i>of her
fœtus.</i> (S, K.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3-  [<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">الاَكِلُ</span> is erroneously put, in
the CK, for <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">الآكِلُ</span>, in a sense explained below.]

